error[E0277]: `clear()` needs a record whose all-zero bytes are certainly valid (`ZERO_IS_VALID`), and this record's are not
  --> tests/ui/fail/81_clear_zero_invalid_record.rs:76:12
   |
76 |     status.clear();
   |            ^^^^^ `clear()` is unavailable on this record
   |
   = help: the trait `ClearableState` is not implemented for `ZeroInvalid`
   = note: a field with no all-zero value, for example a scalar enum without a `= 0` variant, makes `ZERO_IS_VALID` false; give the enum a zero variant or wrap the field in `Option<_>`, which is absent when all-zero
   = note: a record holding an externally tagged payload can be cleared only when the zero tag is claimed and every variant payload is zero-valid, even where `ZERO_IS_VALID` is true
   = help: the trait `ClearableState` is implemented for `ZeroValid`
   = note: required for `Gate<'_, ZeroInvalid>` to implement `ZeroClear`
